#
# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the host tests (Makefile, LEAKS on Linux).
# Each entry is an allocation of the harness's own that lives as long as the
# process by design and is never freed, matched by a harness function on its
# allocation stack; no entry names the firmware's code. Everything else a test
# allocates and loses is a leak and fails the run, so the firmware, which
# allocates nothing (docs/misra.md, tests/firmware/test_no_dynamic_memory.py),
# has nothing here.
#
# A simulated board per test, whose tasks are frozen and never joined
# (harness/sim.h), and the firmware objects Bench boots on it the way
# app_main() does, for the life of the process.
leak:bench::Scope::Scope
leak:bench::Bench::Bench
leak:bench::Bench::boot
# The objects the fakes of ESP-IDF hand the firmware for good (a bus, a device,
# a queue or semaphore under a static create), as
# ESP-IDF allocates them on the device: all made by sim::hold() (harness/sim.cpp).
leak:sim::hold
